    "title": "Document save_ tool action-fold exception for lifecycle actions",
    "description": "## Summary\n\nDocument an exception to the `save_` tool naming convention in the gitlab-mcp-tool-builder skill. Tools prefixed `save_` can now fold non-field-mutation lifecycle actions (like `retry` or `cancel`) behind an `action` parameter when those actions operate on the same resource the tool creates, rather than requiring a separate dedicated tool. This pattern was discovered and used while building the `save_pipeline` MCP tool in !248323. Version bumped from 1.6.1 to 1.6.2 to satisfy the skills version check.\n\n## How to test locally\n\n1. Run `BASE_REF=origin/master scripts/lint/check-skills-version-bump.sh` and confirm it exits with status 0.\n2. Commit the change locally and verify that the pre-commit hooks pass, specifically the `skills-parity` check which confirms `.claude/skills` and `.agents/skills` remain synchronized via the symlink.",
